    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0423" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1536.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sullivan</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-30T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1915—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Johnston. In accordance with recommendations of Johnston and Baxter, telegram
                    was sent yesterday by Bureau of Insular Affairs instructing Baxter to pay over
                    to Dominican Government after April 1 only amounts to which it is entitled by
                    treaty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
